tter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">Don't Miss: Our Quarterly Report on Ad Economics</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td><img src=\"https://images.axios.com/NP5HaRRtApPuk5_zb5ad6LOPqGA=/2026/07/17/1784303002645.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" /></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"15\" style=\"height: 15px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75;  font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<p><strong>Media Trends Executive</strong> just released its exclusive quarterly report on the forces reshaping ad economics.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Built for executives, it pairs expert reporting with essential data and charts to show where ad dollars are moving next.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>🔒 <strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/46973617.242893/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL21lZGlhLXRyZW5kcy1leGVjdXRpdmU_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09YWQmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW10ZV9hY3F1aXNpdGlvbiZ1dG1fYXVkaWVuY2U9bXVsdGkmdXRtX2NvbnRlbnQ9MjAyNjA3UTJyZXBvcnQmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd52d89cf\" target=\"_blank\">Become a member</a></strong> today to unlock this exclusive Media Trends Executive report.</p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0; border-bottom: 10px solid #f5f5f5;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td height=\"10\" style=\"height: 10px; font-size: 0;\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td style=\"padding: 20px 3.5% 10px; line-height: 1.5;\"><span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size: 27px; font-family: 'gorditamedium', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px; line-height: 1.5;\">\r\n2. 🏰 Parting shot: Castle cruise\r\n</span></td></tr>\r\n<tr><td class=\"v\" style=\"padding: 0 3.5%; line-height: 1.75; font-size: 17px; font-family: Georgia, serif; line-height: 1.75; color: #222222; letter-spacing: -0.1px;\">\r\n<div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/mbV4QSmjukJbuz8dIuFQTfH8GQw=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/08/10/1786375007504.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/mbV4QSmjukJbuz8dIuFQTfH8GQw=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/08/10/1786375007504.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">Photo: Steve Ward</div><p><strong>Steve Ward</strong> of Plymouth, Mich., shares this view of the Gravensteen while vacationing in Ghent, Belgium, earlier this month.</p><ul><li><strong>The medieval castle</strong> dates to 1180, and once served as the residence of the Counts of Flanders.</li></ul><p><strong>🍺 Ward also points</strong> to a favorite bit of local lore: In 1949, students occupied the empty castle in protest of a new beer tax, staying overnight before the standoff ended peacefully the next morning.</p>\r\n</td></tr>\r\n<tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/46973617.242893/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNzI4MDY3OWEtZGM0OS00Yzc0LWI3YmUtM2YwNTQ1YzYyMDJmLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QyJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkyJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCd2d46041\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/46973617.242893/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_dGV4dD0lRjAlOUYlOE